INFO  [Claude Code] ### Root Cause Analysis:
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] The issues were caused by Diffblue Cover attempting to use the static `open()` factory methods to construct test instances. These factory methods attempt to establish actual network connections (UDP/TCP sockets), which fail during test construction with `UnresolvedAddressException`.
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] ### Solution:
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] By making the constructors public, Diffblue Cover can now:
INFO  [Claude Code] - Directly instantiate these classes using their constructors
INFO  [Claude Code] - Pass mock or null transport objects (as already demonstrated in the existing test files)
INFO  [Claude Code] - Avoid the network connection attempts that occur in the `open()` factory methods
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] The constructors accept already-constructed transport objects, which can be created with null channels for testing purposes (e.g., `new MoldUDP64Server(null, "Session")`), allowing tests to be generated without requiring actual network resources.
